{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1459391-m20-avatar-and-quintessence-usage","id":1459391,"title":"M20 Avatar and Quintessence usage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-08T19:48:28-07:00","id":1459391,"title":"M20 Avatar and Quintessence usage","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused about how the Avatar ratings above 3 work, as per the core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 You can spend Quintessence to reduce the difficulty<br /> of a magick casting roll. <b>Each point spent reduces that<br /> difficulty by 1, to a maximum reduction of -3.</b><br /> \u2022 That said, <b>the amount of Quintessence you can spend at<br /> one time is limited by your mage\u2019s Avatar Trait</b>. A character<br /> with Avatar 2, for example, may spend or absorb only two<br /> Quintessence points within a single turn. </div> </div> </div>So if I can not spend more than 3 points casting... What is it good to have Avatar 4 or 5? Are there other ways to spend more than 3 Quintessence for casting? Are there other usages for Quintessence?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T20:00:23-07:00","id":1459392,"title":"","content":"The -3 limit to reductions applies to ALL difficulty reductions. Moreover, difficulty reductions cancel out difficulty increases. The ability to spend 4 or 5 Quintessence is good for when you're trying to both make up for lots of factors working against you, AND push the difficulty even lower. Like, if you're operating at a difficulty +3, you need to spend 3 Quintessence to get the Effect down to normal, and a further 2 Quint to get it down to -2.<br /> <br /> For high level Effects, you really want to get your difficulty as low as possible, just to offset the naturally high base difficulty of the Effect itself. Let alone try to pull it off while ALSO working under less than ideal conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T02:50:52-07:00","id":1459414,"title":"","content":"M20 cut back on them a bit, but there are effects that require Quintessence as part of the effect. So if you need to spend Quintessence (such as infusing it into a weapon so it does Agg damage), having Avatar 4+ means you can max your reduction of the difficulty on the casting roll to empower the weapon and pay the requisite price.<br /> <br /> There are also a few variants of countermagic that cost Quintessence, and some of those don't have any cap, so high Avatar could allow a greater protective effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T01:50:58-07:00","id":1459634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1459391-m20-avatar-and-quintessence-usage#post1459391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I can not spend more than 3 points casting... What is it good to have Avatar 4 or 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple, it's -3 from *base* difficulty, not *total* difficulty adjustment.<br /> That means, if you are in a circumstance where you have a +2 difficulty increase (bad tass resonance, distractions, unfamiliar instruments, juggling effects etc.) you can *still* drop the diff down to -3 from base with avatar 5. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}